    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14079" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποτολμ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make a bold venture upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.67
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐπιχειρῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					7.28
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.131
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.45.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.233
			</span></i>, etc.:—pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			 in act. sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἐλευθερίας
				λίαν ἀποτετολμημένης</span> too <i>presumptuous</i>
			liberty, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				701b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
				25
			</span></i>: in pass. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰπεῖν τὰ νῦν ἀποτετ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					503b
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποτολμᾷ καὶ λέγει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
					10.20
				</span></i>
			: c.acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναίρεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					7.8.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
